A||||12||TRiAD||TRiAD's epic journey, pt deux||||1||
Z||000000||TRiAD||12-09-2001||08:59 PM||||Well, Daniel (FieroAutoXdb or something similar, sorry) came over this afternoon, and REALLY helped out on my car...drove 1.5hrs each way too!<P>He let me take a ride in his duke (it's nice to drive one of these that WORKS! LOL!), then we hit the GT hard...<P>HE helped finish the clutch pedal R&R, and here's a pic of the 2 pedals side by side...I don't think it was bent, but it needed done anyway...<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pedal-side-by-side-1.jpg"> <P><BR>When we tried to bleed the clutch system, we discovered what is likely the real problem...<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mastercyl1.jpg"> <P>You see, there's now fluid all over the area of the master cylinder...<P>...The BIG arrow is...<P>...a patch of electrical tape that was stuck to the bottom ofthe master cylinder, where there's a crack in the housing. This is most likely what is causing the inability to shift when the car is running, and the "creeping" in gear, even when the clutch is depressed. <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Master-cylinder-evidence-.jpg"> <P>The previous owner denies any knowledge of this, so it was apparently like this for months...<P>Anyway, anyone know a cheap supplier for a complete master cylinder? ...Or have one to donate?         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Thanks!<P><BR>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0QwBlO10XBwtwZZqI3Om69ptsim8sbgsv6htbwTK5nTjOTXqfhFmE7PufW3uqtRZBdEgZz0PO6pMaCru!KJ*SRcaq8o*iHyw9Pc8KZEv!vcY/Signature-pic-small.jpg">            <BR><B><I><FONT COLOR="blue">Project MR1 ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</B> ~ Photoshop rendition of planned modifications</I></FONT><P>[thanks to maryjane for the pics...]<p>[This message has been edited by TRiAD (edited 12-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||TRiAD||12-09-2001||09:09 PM||||duhhhh, which way did he go, Dorge, which way did he go?!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><p>[This message has been edited by TRiAD (edited 12-09-2001).]||||reg||8
Z||000002||FieroMaster88||12-09-2001||09:37 PM||||There is a guy here in MI who had NOS GM parts for sale.  Got my master and slave cylinder from him.  Low prices and a good guy to work with!<P>Go here to check it out: <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum4/HTML/005325.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum4/HTML/005325.html</A> <P>Tell him what you need and he will hook you up!  <P>Hope this helps!  <P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieromaster88sig.gif">  <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>Not your ordinary 88 coupe!||||reg||1
